ml.ws/jaxws-rt` entries already in `metadata/` (same repo, same `4.0.5` release train, same Maven reactor build as `rt-fi`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"coordinates\" : \"com.sun.xml.ws:rt-fi:4.0.5\",\n  \"repository-url\" : \"https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/metro-jax-ws\",\n  \"source-code-url\" : \"https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/com/sun/xml/ws/rt-fi/$version$/rt-fi-$version$-sources.jar\",\n  \"test-code-url\" : \"https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/metro-jax-ws/tree/$version$/jaxws-ri/runtime/rt-fi/src/test\",\n  \"documentation-url\" : \"https://javadoc.io/doc/com.sun.xml.ws/rt-fi/$version$/index.html\",\n  \"description\" : \"The rt-fi module is the Fast Infoset integration for the Eclipse Metro JAX-WS reference implementation of Jakarta XML Web Services. It supplies the codecs and content-negotiation logic that let JAX-WS clients and endpoints exchange SOAP messages encoded in the compact Fast Infoset binary XML format instead of plain text XML.\"\n}\n```\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- `com.sun.xml.ws:rt-fi` is a sibling reactor module of `com.sun.xml.ws:rt`/`jaxws-rt` inside the **eclipse-ee4j/metro-jax-ws** repo — same group, same release tag, built by the same multi-module Maven POM, so the sources-jar/javadoc.io URL patterns that already work for its siblings carry over directly.\n- \"Fast Infoset\" (also seen in this repo as `com.sun.xml.fastinfoset:FastInfoset`) is a W3C binary XML format; `rt-fi` is the adapter layer that plugs that encoder into JAX-WS's SOAP message pipeline — it's not usable standalone, only as a runtime extension alongside `rt`/`jaxws-rt`.\n- No language runtime (Kotlin/Groovy/Scala) and no Android/JS-only packaging applies here, so `language` and `not-for-native-image` are correctly left absent — it's a plain JVM artifact, same as its siblings that already have native-image metadata.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nNo fields needed `\"N/A\"` — confidence here comes from direct, in-repo prece